## What

A new `hold_hour` open-trade phone alert: one alert when a long option opened today has been held 60 regular-session minutes, so Isaac re-decides it. It is off until `POSITION_HOLD_ALERTS=true`, which works only with `POSITION_ALERTS_ENABLED=true` as well. It only sends a phone alert. Nothing places, changes or suggests an order.

Why: the [behavior audit](backend/reports/behavior_audit_2026-10-21.md) found that trades held from 1 hour to the same-day close lost $17,558. 53 of those losers had been up ≥10% in their first hour. The audit suggests: "Re-decide any position still open after an hour."

## Behavior (`backend/app/engine/position_alerts.py`)

- **When it fires:** 60 minutes after the first entry fill. An entry before the open counts from 09:30.
- **When it is skipped:**
  - the 60 minutes would land at or after the close (half days come from the calendar);
  - an expiry alert is due within 15 minutes of it (expiry wins);
  - it would be more than 15 minutes late;
  - the position was opened on a prior day.
- **Once per position.** It is recorded with the give-back generation current when it fires. Adding to the position never restarts the clock or re-sends, whether the add comes before or after the alert. This is enforced in `_record` and documented in the module docstring.
- **Message:** for example "Open 60 min, now -$24 (-6%) at a $3.76 mid, bid $3.74, best seen by the alert watch +$48 (+12%). 1 contract open. Re-decide: close, trim, or set your exit."
  - It uses the existing Tradier midpoint and the quote-age/spread guards.
  - A quote that can't be judged still sends, with "no reliable quote" (plus the bid if it is fresh).
- **Delivery:** the existing at-most-once outbox, unchanged. Like the expiry alerts, it is not sent after the close.
- **No migration:** `kind` is a plain string column.
- **Other files:** `KINDS`/model comment, `.env.example` (both flags), the trade page label "Open an hour: re-decide", and the feature map.

## Tests

- `tests/test_position_alerts.py`: 32 passed. The 11 new tests cover:
  - fires at 60 minutes, and not before;
  - a pre-open entry counts from 09:30;
  - half day: skipped when the hour lands after the early close, and still fires before it;
  - once per position across adds;
  - skipped when more than 15 minutes late;
  - expiry wins in the overlap (plus `hold_due` boundary cases);
  - off without either flag;
  - an unjudgeable quote still sends;
  - at-most-once delivery.
- `e2e/trade-phone-alerts.spec.ts` (with a `hold_hour` row added): 2 passed. The phone-width screenshot was checked.

Tier 1, alerts only, with no fills/FIFO/money semantics. One independent review found nothing material, and its small test gaps were addressed. Isaac merges. No VPS settings were changed.

