Builds on #175, which is merged.

## What changes
- On a report, the care team can **ask about this report**, as in a clinical evidence search. Claude:
  - reads the report as a cited document;
  - searches the medical literature on a fixed list of trusted sites (`nih.gov`, `fda.gov`, `cdc.gov`, `who.int`, Cochrane and major journals).
- Each part of the answer has a numbered source: a quote of the report, or a page of the literature with its link.
- The answer streams to the page. Three suggested questions help a first-time user.
- The care team keeps the questions and answers (the 10 newest show). The person does not see them.
- The assistant answers; the clinician decides. The instructions tell Claude:
  - to say when the evidence is weak or missing;
  - that a change after the start does not prove cause;
  - not to make the treatment decision.

## How
- `lib/care-team/assistant.ts` (no server code):
  - the report as plain text, without the person's or the clinician's name. Values from the file go as they are; only calculated values are rounded;
  - the trusted sites;
  - the answer built from stream events. The page and the server use the same code.
- `lib/care-team/ask.ts` makes the Claude API call with the official SDK (`@anthropic-ai/sdk`):
  - model `claude-opus-5-5`, effort `medium`;
  - web search `web_search_20260209` with `allowed_domains`, max 4 searches;
  - document citations, and prompt caching of the report;
  - server-side refusal fallbacks (`fallbacks: "default"`);
  - paused turns (`pause_turn`) are resumed.
- It also keeps the question log, with a daily limit of 50 questions for each company. Every demo visitor shares one clinician account. The count and the insert run under an advisory lock for the company, so questions asked at the same time cannot pass the limit together.
- `POST /api/care-team/reports/{id}/questions` streams JSON lines. Only clinicians of the report's care team can use it; all others get 404.
- Migration `20261023040000_table_report_questions.sql`: the care team reads the log, and only the server writes it.

## Health data
Health data goes to the Claude API only under a business associate agreement. Until there is one, the assistant works only on the demo clinic, whose values are made up, and only when `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set. Without the key, the panel does not show.

## Tests
- Unit (`tests/unit/care-team/assistant.test.ts`), with a fake client:
  - the report document and its numbers;
  - the source numbering;
  - the request (model, trusted sites, fallbacks, cited and cached document, no name);
  - a paused turn;
  - a refusal.
- DB (`tests/db/report-assistant.test.ts`):
  - when the assistant is available;
  - who reads the log;
  - that clients cannot write it;
  - the daily limit, also with 20 questions asked at the same time.
- Browser:
  - a mock of the Claude API (`tests/e2e/mock-claude.mjs`) streams one answer with two sources. Playwright and CI start it, so no outside service is contacted;
  - the tour asks a question before the sign-off (new step `clinician-4`; sign-off is now `clinician-5`);
  - a test checks that a person outside the care team gets 404.
- New dependency: `@anthropic-ai/sdk`. pnpm also re-resolved two peer links of `@better-auth/oauth-provider` (zod, jose) and `@babel/runtime` (7.28 → 7.29). The auth and OAuth database tests pass.

Ran locally: type check, lint, unit (340 passed), DB (121 passed), build, and browser tests (37 passed).
